# Button Fix Order Table

## Summary

Use this as the cleanup order for the remaining generic buttons. The lists below show the actual buttons so each one can be tweaked individually.  pure white buttons are to be considered unclassified and should be assigned to the best fitting semantic class per the intent of the action. The hover colors are recommended, but feel free to suggest a different choice if you think it better suits the intent of the action.

## Fix Order

| Fix order | Button group             | Associated color | What to use it for                                                                         |
| --------- | ------------------------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 1         | `btn-refresh`            | TEAL             | Reload, refresh, and reload-state actions.                                                 |
| 2         | `primary`                | Red - primary    | Main action buttons such as create, save, import, and open-primary-view.                   |
| 3         | `alt`                    | Blue - tertiary  | Secondary navigation, back, close, prev, next, and zoom controls.                          |
| 4         | `danger`                 | PURPLE           | Logout or destructive actions.                                                             |
| 5         | `needs class assignment` | see  below       | Buttons still relying on the generic fallback; assign the right semantic class per intent. |
| 6         | `info`                   | lt. blue         | View/navigate to info section, page, or modal                                              |

